      <div class="page-container bio-grid-wrap">
        <div class="bio-grid">
          <div class="bio-text-col">
            <div class="bio-copy">
              <p>
                <strong>S. Khavin</strong> is a final-year Computer Science Engineering student at
                Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Chennai, and an independent
                researcher studying mechanistic interpretability, computational geometry in residual
                streams, and training-free efficient inference.
              </p>
              <p>
                His work tests which circuits and representations inside language and
                vision-language models are causally necessary versus geometrically epiphenomenal,
                using those maps for zero-training sparse routing, proactive O(1) KV-cache eviction,
                and linear-time video memory graphs.
              </p>
            </div>

